(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[8] = [{"v":1,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"किं तद्ब्रह्म किमध्यात्मं किं कर्म पुरुषोत्तम ।\nअधिभूतं च किं प्रोक्तमधिदैवं किमुच्यते ॥","iast":"kiṃ tadbrahma kimadhyātmaṃ kiṃ karma puruṣottama |\nadhibhūtaṃ ca kiṃ proktamadhidaivaṃ kimucyate ||","read":"kim tadbrahma kimadhyaatmam kim karma purushottama |\nadhibhootam cha kim proktamadhidaivam kimuchyate ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: What is that Eternal, what Self -knowledge, what Action, O Purushottama? And what is declared to be the knowledge of the Elements, what is called the knowledge of the Shining Ones?","en2":"What is that Brahman, what is Adhyâtma, what is Karma, O best of Purushas? What is called Adhibhuta, and what Adhidaiva?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna what the Eternal is, what knowledge of the Self is, and what action is. He also asks what knowledge of the elements and of the Shining Ones means."},{"v":2,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अधियज्ञः कथं कोऽत्र देहेऽस्मिन्मधुसूदन ।\nप्रयाणकाले च कथं ज्ञेयोऽसि नियतात्मभिः ॥","iast":"adhiyajñaḥ kathaṃ ko’tra dehe’sminmadhusūdana |\nprayāṇakāle ca kathaṃ jñeyo’si niyatātmabhiḥ ||","read":"adhiyajnah katham ko'tra dehe'sminmadhusoodana |\nprayaanakaale cha katham jneyo'si niyataatmabhih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"What is the knowledge of Sacrifice in this body, and how, O, Madhusûdana? And how, at the time of forthgoing art Thou known by the Self -controlled?","en2":"Who, and in what way, is Adhiyajna here in this body, O destroyer of Madhu? And how art Thou known at the time of death, by the self-controlled?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Arjuna asks Krishna what sacrifice in this body is, and how it works. He also asks how people with self-control know Krishna at the time of death."},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"अक्षरं ब्रह्म परमं स्वभावोऽध्यात्ममुच्यते ।\nभूतभावोद्भवकरो विसर्गः कर्मसंज्ञितः ॥","iast":"akṣaraṃ brahma paramaṃ svabhāvo’dhyātmamucyate |\nbhūtabhāvodbhavakaro visargaḥ karmasaṃjñitaḥ ||","read":"aksharam brahma paramam svabhaavo'dhyaatmamuchyate |\nbhootabhaavodbhavakaro visargah karmasamjnitah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: The indestructible, the supreme is the Eternal; His essential nature is called Self -knowledge; the emanation that causes the birth of beings is named Action;","en2":"The Imperishable is the Supreme Brahman. Its dwelling in each individual body is called Adhyâtma; the offering in sacrifice which causes the genesis and support of beings, is called Karma.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the Eternal is the highest, the one that cannot be destroyed. Its nature is called knowledge of the Self. What brings beings to birth is called action."},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अधिभूतं क्षरो भावः पुरुषश्चाधिदैवतम् ।\nअधियज्ञोऽहमेवात्र देहे देहभृतां वर ॥","iast":"adhibhūtaṃ kṣaro bhāvaḥ puruṣaścādhidaivatam |\nadhiyajño’hamevātra dehe dehabhṛtāṃ vara ||","read":"adhibhootam ksharo bhaavah purushashchaadhidaivatam |\nadhiyajno'hamevaatra dehe dehabhritaam vara ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Knowledge of the Elements concerns My perishable nature, and knowledge of the Shining Ones concerns the life-giving energy; the knowledge of Sacrifice tells of Me, as wearing the body, O best of living beings.","en2":"The perishable adjunct is the Adhibhuta, and the Indweller is the Adhidaivata; I alone am the Adhiyajna here in this body, O best of the embodied.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the elements are the part of things that perishes. The Shining Ones are about the life within. And sacrifice, here in the body, is about Krishna himself."},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अन्तकाले च मामेव स्मरन्मुक्त्वा कलेवरम् ।\nयः प्रयाति स मद्भावं याति नास्त्यत्र संशयः ॥","iast":"antakāle ca māmeva smaranmuktvā kalevaram |\nyaḥ prayāti sa madbhāvaṃ yāti nāstyatra saṃśayaḥ ||","read":"antakaale cha maameva smaranmuktvaa kalevaram |\nyah prayaati sa madbhaavam yaati naastyatra samshayah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"And he who, casting off the body, goeth forth thinking upon Me only at the time of the end, he entereth into My being: there is no doubt of that.","en2":"And he, who at the time of death, meditating on Me alone, goes forth, leaving the body, attains My Being: there is no doubt about this.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that whoever leaves the body at the time of death thinking only of him reaches the very being of Krishna. There is no doubt about this."},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यं यं वापि स्मरन्भावं त्यजत्यन्ते कलेवरम् ।\nतं तमेवैति कौन्तेय सदा तद्भावभावितः ॥","iast":"yaṃ yaṃ vāpi smaranbhāvaṃ tyajatyante kalevaram |\ntaṃ tamevaiti kaunteya sadā tadbhāvabhāvitaḥ ||","read":"yam yam vaapi smaranbhaavam tyajatyante kalevaram |\ntam tamevaiti kaunteya sadaa tadbhaavabhaavitah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whosoever at the end abandoneth the body, thinking upon any being, to that being only he goeth, O Kaunteya, ever to that conformed in nature.","en2":"Remembering whatever object, at the end, he leaves the body, that alone is reached by him, O son of Kunti, (because) of his constant thought of that object.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that whatever a person thinks of when leaving the body at the end, that is what he goes to, because his mind has always been turned to it."},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु मामनुस्मर युध्य च ।\nमय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्मामेवैष्यस्यसंशयम् ॥","iast":"tasmātsarveṣu kāleṣu māmanusmara yudhya ca |\nmayyarpitamanobuddhirmāmevaiṣyasyasaṃśayam ||","read":"tasmaatsarveshu kaaleshu maamanusmara yudhya cha |\nmayyarpitamanobuddhirmaamevaishyasyasamshayam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore at all times think upon Me only and fight. With mind and Reason set on Me, without doubt thou shalt come to Me.","en2":"Therefore, at all times, constantly remember Me, and fight. With mind and intellect absorbed, in Me, thou shalt doubtless come to Me.","en2r":null,"rv":"Editions differ here (asaṃśayam / asaṃśayaḥ); this is the vulgate reading.","kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna to think of him at all times, and fight. With his mind and understanding fixed on Krishna, Arjuna will surely come to him."},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अभ्यासयोगयुक्तेन चेतसा नान्यगामिना ।\nपरमं पुरुषं दिव्यं याति पार्थानुचिन्तयन् ॥","iast":"abhyāsayogayuktena cetasā nānyagāminā |\nparamaṃ puruṣaṃ divyaṃ yāti pārthānucintayan ||","read":"abhyaasayogayuktena chetasaa naanyagaaminaa |\nparamam purusham divyam yaati paarthaanuchintayan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"With the mind not wandering after aught else, harmonised by continual practice, constantly meditating, O Pârtha, one goeth to the Spirit supreme, divine.","en2":"With the mind not moving towards anything else, made steadfast by the method of habitual meditation, and dwelling on the Supreme, Resplendent Purusha, O son of Prithâ, one goes to Him.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that someone whose mind does not wander to anything else, made steady by constant practice and meditation, goes to the highest divine Spirit."},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कविं पुराणमनुशासितार ।\nमणोरणीयांसमनुस्मरेद्यः ।\nसर्वस्य धातारमचिन्त्यरूप ।\nमादित्यवर्णं तमसः परस्तात् ॥","iast":"kaviṃ purāṇamanuśāsitāra |\nmaṇoraṇīyāṃsamanusmaredyaḥ |\nsarvasya dhātāramacintyarūpa |\nmādityavarṇaṃ tamasaḥ parastāt ||","read":"kavim puraanamanushaasitaara |\nmanoraneeyaamsamanusmaredyah |\nsarvasya dhaataaramachintyaroopa |\nmaadityavarnam tamasah parastaat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who thinketh upon the Ancient, the Omniscient, the All-Ruler, minuter than the minute, the supporter of all, of form unimaginable, refulgent as the sun beyond the darkness,","en2":"The Omniscient, the Ancient, the Overruler, minuter than an atom, the Sustainer of all, of form inconceivable, self-luminous like the sun, and beyond the darkness of Mâyâ—he who meditates on Him thus, at the time of death, full of devotion, with the mind unmoving, and also by the power of Yoga, fixing the whole Prâna betwixt the eye-brows, he goes to that Supreme, Resplendent Purusha.","en2r":"8.9-10","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna describes the one to think about: the Ancient One, who knows all and rules all, smaller than the smallest, holding up everything, with a form no one can imagine, shining like the sun beyond the darkness."},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रयाणकाले मनसाऽचलेन ।\nभक्त्या युक्तो योगबलेन चैव ।\nभ्रुवोर्मध्ये प्राणमावेश्य सम्यक् ।\nस तं परं पुरुषमुपैति दिव्यम् ॥","iast":"prayāṇakāle manasā’calena |\nbhaktyā yukto yogabalena caiva |\nbhruvormadhye prāṇamāveśya samyak |\nsa taṃ paraṃ puruṣamupaiti divyam ||","read":"prayaanakaale manasaa'chalena |\nbhaktyaa yukto yogabalena chaiva |\nbhruvormadhye praanamaaveshya samyak |\nsa tam param purushamupaiti divyam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"In the time of forthgoing, with unshaken mind, fixed in devotion, by the power of yoga drawing together his life-breath in the centre of the two eyebrows, he goeth to this Spirit, supreme, divine.","en2":"The Omniscient, the Ancient, the Overruler, minuter than an atom, the Sustainer of all, of form inconceivable, self-luminous like the sun, and beyond the darkness of Mâyâ—he who meditates on Him thus, at the time of death, full of devotion, with the mind unmoving, and also by the power of Yoga, fixing the whole Prâna betwixt the eye-brows, he goes to that Supreme, Resplendent Purusha.","en2r":"8.9-10","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that at the time of death, a person full of devotion, with a still mind, who draws his life-breath to the point between the eyebrows, goes to the highest divine Spirit."},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदक्षरं वेदविदो वदन्ति ।\nविशन्ति यद्यतयो वीतरागाः ।\nयदिच्छन्तो ब्रह्मचर्यं चरन्ति ।\nतत्ते पदं संग्रहेण प्रवक्ष्ये ॥","iast":"yadakṣaraṃ vedavido vadanti |\nviśanti yadyatayo vītarāgāḥ |\nyadicchanto brahmacaryaṃ caranti |\ntatte padaṃ saṃgraheṇa pravakṣye ||","read":"yadaksharam vedavido vadanti |\nvishanti yadyatayo veetaraagaah |\nyadichchhanto brahmacharyam charanti |\ntatte padam samgrahena pravakshye ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which is declared indestructible by the Veda-knowers, that which the controlled and passion-free enter, that desiring which Brahmacharya is performed, that path I will declare to thee with brevity.","en2":"What the knowers of the Veda speak of as Imperishable, what the self-controlled (Sannyâsins), freed from attachment enter, and to gain which goal they live the life of a Brahmachârin, that I shall declare unto thee in brief.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says he will briefly describe what those who know the Veda call the Imperishable. The self-controlled, free from attachment, enter it, and people live lives of strict discipline to reach it."},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वद्वाराणि संयम्य मनो हृदि निरुध्य च ।\nमूर्ध्न्याधायात्मनः प्राणमास्थितो योगधारणाम् ॥","iast":"sarvadvārāṇi saṃyamya mano hṛdi nirudhya ca |\nmūrdhnyādhāyātmanaḥ prāṇamāsthito yogadhāraṇām ||","read":"sarvadvaaraani samyamya mano hridi nirudhya cha |\nmoordhnyaadhaayaatmanah praanamaasthito yogadhaaranaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"All the gates closed, the mind confined in the heart, the life-breath fixed in his own head, concentrated by yoga,","en2":"Controlling all the senses, confining the mind in the heart, drawing the Prâna into the head, occupied in the practice of concentration, uttering the one-syllabled \"Om\"—the Brahman, and meditating on Me;—he who so departs, leaving the body, attains the Supreme Goal.","en2r":"8.12-13","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna describes a person who closes all the gates of the senses, keeps his mind in the heart, holds his life-breath in his head, and stays fixed in concentration."},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ओमित्येकाक्षरं ब्रह्म व्याहरन्मामनुस्मरन् ।\nयः प्रयाति त्यजन्देहं स याति परमां गतिम् ॥","iast":"omityekākṣaraṃ brahma vyāharanmāmanusmaran |\nyaḥ prayāti tyajandehaṃ sa yāti paramāṃ gatim ||","read":"omityekaaksharam brahma vyaaharanmaamanusmaran |\nyah prayaati tyajandeham sa yaati paramaam gatim ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\"Aum!\" the one syllabled Eternal, reciting, thinking upon Me, he who goeth forth, abandoning the body, he goeth on the highest path.","en2":"Controlling all the senses, confining the mind in the heart, drawing the Prâna into the head, occupied in the practice of concentration, uttering the one-syllabled \"Om\"—the Brahman, and meditating on Me;—he who so departs, leaving the body, attains the Supreme Goal.","en2r":"8.12-13","rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that a person who leaves the body saying the one syllable that is the Eternal, and thinking of Krishna, goes on the highest path."},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनन्यचेताः सततं यो मां स्मरति नित्यशः ।\nतस्याहं सुलभः पार्थ नित्ययुक्तस्य योगिनः ॥","iast":"ananyacetāḥ satataṃ yo māṃ smarati nityaśaḥ |\ntasyāhaṃ sulabhaḥ pārtha nityayuktasya yoginaḥ ||","read":"ananyachetaah satatam yo maam smarati nityashah |\ntasyaaham sulabhah paartha nityayuktasya yoginah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who constantly thinketh upon Me, not thinking ever of another, of him I am easily reached, O Pârtha, of this ever-harmonised Yogî.","en2":"I am easily attainable by that ever-steadfast Yogin who remembers Me constantly and daily, with a single mind, O son of Prithâ.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he is easy to reach for the steady person who thinks of him always, every day, and never of anything else."},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मामुपेत्य पुनर्जन्म दुःखालयमशाश्वतम् ।\nनाप्नुवन्ति महात्मानः संसिद्धिं परमां गताः ॥","iast":"māmupetya punarjanma duḥkhālayamaśāśvatam |\nnāpnuvanti mahātmānaḥ saṃsiddhiṃ paramāṃ gatāḥ ||","read":"maamupetya punarjanma duhkhaalayamashaashvatam |\nnaapnuvanti mahaatmaanah samsiddhim paramaam gataah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Having come to Me, these Mahâtmâs come not again to birth, the place of pain, non-eternal; they have gone to the highest bliss.","en2":"Reaching the highest perfection, and having attained Me, the great-souled ones are no more subject to re-birth—which is the home of pain, and ephemeral.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that great souls who have come to him are not born again. Birth is a place of pain that does not last. They have reached the highest joy."},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन ।\nमामुपेत्य तु कौन्तेय पुनर्जन्म न विद्यते ॥","iast":"ābrahmabhuvanāllokāḥ punarāvartino’rjuna |\nmāmupetya tu kaunteya punarjanma na vidyate ||","read":"aabrahmabhuvanaallokaah punaraavartino'rjuna |\nmaamupetya tu kaunteya punarjanma na vidyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The worlds, beginning with the world of Brahmâ, they come and go, O Arjuna; but he who cometh unto Me, O Kaunteya, he knoweth birth no more.","en2":"All the worlds, O Arjuna, including the realm of Brahmâ, are subject to return, but after attaining Me, O son of Kunti, there is no re-birth.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that all the worlds come and go. But a person who comes to Krishna is not born again."},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सहस्रयुगपर्यन्तमहर्यद्ब्रह्मणो विदुः ।\nरात्रिं युगसहस्रान्तां तेऽहोरात्रविदो जनाः ॥","iast":"sahasrayugaparyantamaharyadbrahmaṇo viduḥ |\nrātriṃ yugasahasrāntāṃ te’horātravido janāḥ ||","read":"sahasrayugaparyantamaharyadbrahmano viduh |\nraatrim yugasahasraantaam te'horaatravido janaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The people who know the day of Brahmâ, a thousand ages in duration, and the night a thousand ages in ending, they know day and night.","en2":"They who know (the true measure of) day and night, know the day of Brahmâ, which ends in a thousand Yugas, and the night which (also) ends in a thousand Yugas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that people who know of the great day that lasts a thousand ages, and the night that lasts a thousand ages, truly know what day and night are."},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अव्यक्ताद्व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवन्त्यहरागमे ।\nरात्र्यागमे प्रलीयन्ते तत्रैवाव्यक्तसंज्ञके ॥","iast":"avyaktādvyaktayaḥ sarvāḥ prabhavantyaharāgame |\nrātryāgame pralīyante tatraivāvyaktasaṃjñake ||","read":"avyaktaadvyaktayah sarvaah prabhavantyaharaagame |\nraatryaagame praleeyante tatraivaavyaktasamjnake ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"From the unmanifested all the manifested stream forth at the coming of day; at the coming of night they dissolve, even in That called the unmanifested.","en2":"At the approach of (Brahmâ's) day, all manifestations proceed from the unmanifested state; at the approach of night, they merge verily into that alone, which is called the unmanifested.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that when that day comes, all things that can be seen come out of the unseen. When night comes, they melt back into the unseen."},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"भूतग्रामः स एवायं भूत्वा भूत्वा प्रलीयते ।\nरात्र्यागमेऽवशः पार्थ प्रभवत्यहरागमे ॥","iast":"bhūtagrāmaḥ sa evāyaṃ bhūtvā bhūtvā pralīyate |\nrātryāgame’vaśaḥ pārtha prabhavatyaharāgame ||","read":"bhootagraamah sa evaayam bhootvaa bhootvaa praleeyate |\nraatryaagame'vashah paartha prabhavatyaharaagame ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This multitude of beings, going forth repeatedly, is dissolved at the coming of night: by ordination, O Pârtha, it streams forth at the coming of day.","en2":"The very same multitude of beings (that existed in the preceding day of Brahmâ), being born again and again, merge, in spite of themselves, O son of Prithâ, (into the unmanifested), at the approach of night, and re-manifest at the approach of day.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that the same crowd of beings is born again and again. When night comes it melts away, not by its own choice, and when day comes it appears again."},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"परस्तस्मात्तु भावोऽन्योऽव्यक्तोऽव्यक्तात्सनातनः ।\nयः स सर्वेषु भूतेषु नश्यत्सु न विनश्यति ॥","iast":"parastasmāttu bhāvo’nyo’vyakto’vyaktātsanātanaḥ |\nyaḥ sa sarveṣu bhūteṣu naśyatsu na vinaśyati ||","read":"parastasmaattu bhaavo'nyo'vyakto'vyaktaatsanaatanah |\nyah sa sarveshu bhooteshu nashyatsu na vinashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore verily there existeth, higher than that unmanifested, another unmanifested, eternal, which in the destroying of all beings, is not destroyed.","en2":"But beyond this unmanifested, there is that other Unmanifested, Eternal Existence—That which is not destroyed at the destruction of all beings.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that beyond this unseen state there is another unseen one that is eternal. When all beings are destroyed, it is not destroyed."},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अव्यक्तोऽक्षर इत्युक्तस्तमाहुः परमां गतिम् ।\nयं प्राप्य न निवर्तन्ते तद्धाम परमं मम ॥","iast":"avyakto’kṣara ityuktastamāhuḥ paramāṃ gatim |\nyaṃ prāpya na nivartante taddhāma paramaṃ mama ||","read":"avyakto'kshara ityuktastamaahuh paramaam gatim |\nyam praapya na nivartante taddhaama paramam mama ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That unmanifested, \"the Indestructible,\" It is called; It is named the highest Path. They who reach It return not. That is My supreme abode.","en2":"What has been called Unmanifested and Imperishable, has been described as the Goal Supreme. That is My highest state, having attained which, there is no return.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says this unseen one is called the Imperishable and the highest goal. Those who reach it do not come back. It is his own highest home."},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पुरुषः स परः पार्थ भक्त्या लभ्यस्त्वनन्यया ।\nयस्यान्तःस्थानि भूतानि येन सर्वमिदं ततम् ॥","iast":"puruṣaḥ sa paraḥ pārtha bhaktyā labhyastvananyayā |\nyasyāntaḥsthāni bhūtāni yena sarvamidaṃ tatam ||","read":"purushah sa parah paartha bhaktyaa labhyastvananyayaa |\nyasyaantahsthaani bhootaani yena sarvamidam tatam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He, the highest Spirit, O Pârtha, may be reached by unswerving devotion to Him alone, in whom all beings abide, by whom all This is pervaded.","en2":"And that Supreme Purusha is attainable, O son of Prithâ, by whole-souled devotion to Him alone, in Whom all beings dwell, and by Whom all this is pervaded.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that the highest Spirit, in whom all beings live and who fills everything, can be reached by whole-hearted devotion to him alone."},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्र काले त्वनावृत्तिमावृत्तिं चैव योगिनः ।\nप्रयाता यान्ति तं कालं वक्ष्यामि भरतर्षभ ॥","iast":"yatra kāle tvanāvṛttimāvṛttiṃ caiva yoginaḥ |\nprayātā yānti taṃ kālaṃ vakṣyāmi bharatarṣabha ||","read":"yatra kaale tvanaavrittimaavrittim chaiva yoginah |\nprayaataa yaanti tam kaalam vakshyaami bharatarshabha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That time wherein going forth Yogîs return not, and also that wherein going forth they return, that time shall I declare to thee, O prince of the Bhâratas.","en2":"Now I shall tell thee, O bull of the Bhâratas, of the time (path) travelling in which, the Yogis return, (and again of that, taking which) they do not return.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that he will now explain the times when those who meditate leave and do not return, and when they leave and do return."},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अग्निर्ज्योतिरहः शुक्लः षण्मासा उत्तरायणम् ।\nतत्र प्रयाता गच्छन्ति ब्रह्म ब्रह्मविदो जनाः ॥","iast":"agnirjyotirahaḥ śuklaḥ ṣaṇmāsā uttarāyaṇam |\ntatra prayātā gacchanti brahma brahmavido janāḥ ||","read":"agnirjyotirahah shuklah shanmaasaa uttaraayanam |\ntatra prayaataa gachchhanti brahma brahmavido janaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Fire, light, day-time, the bright fortnight, the six months of the northern path—then, going forth, the men who know the Eternal go to the Eternal.","en2":"Fire, flame, day-time, the bright fortnight, the six months of the Northern passage of the sun, taking this path, the knowers of Brahman go to Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that those who know the Eternal, and leave in fire, light, daytime, the bright fortnight and the six months of the northern path, go to the Eternal."},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"धूमो रात्रिस्तथा कृष्णः षण्मासा दक्षिणायनम् ।\nतत्र चान्द्रमसं ज्योतिर्योगी प्राप्य निवर्तते ॥","iast":"dhūmo rātristathā kṛṣṇaḥ ṣaṇmāsā dakṣiṇāyanam |\ntatra cāndramasaṃ jyotiryogī prāpya nivartate ||","read":"dhoomo raatristathaa krishnah shanmaasaa dakshinaayanam |\ntatra chaandramasam jyotiryogee praapya nivartate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Smoke, night-time, the dark fortnight also, the six months of the southern path—then the Yogî, obtaining the moonlight, returneth.","en2":"Smoke, night-time, the dark fortnight, the six months of the Southern passage of the sun—taking this path the Yogi, attaining the lunar light, returns.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says that the one who meditates and leaves in smoke, night-time, the dark fortnight and the six months of the southern path reaches the light of the moon, and returns."},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"शुक्लकृष्णे गती ह्येते जगतः शाश्वते मते ।\nएकया यात्यनावृत्तिमन्ययाऽऽवर्तते पुनः ॥","iast":"śuklakṛṣṇe gatī hyete jagataḥ śāśvate mate |\nekayā yātyanāvṛttimanyayā’’vartate punaḥ ||","read":"shuklakrishne gatee hyete jagatah shaashvate mate |\nekayaa yaatyanaavrittimanyayaa''vartate punah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Light and darkness, these are thought to be the world's everlasting paths; by the one he goeth who returneth not, by the other he who returneth again.","en2":"Truly are these bright and dark paths of the world considered eternal: one leads to non-return; by the other, one returns.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the light path and the dark path are thought to be the world's everlasting paths. By one, a person does not return. By the other, he returns again."},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"नैते सृती पार्थ जानन्योगी मुह्यति कश्चन ।\nतस्मात्सर्वेषु कालेषु योगयुक्तो भवार्जुन ॥","iast":"naite sṛtī pārtha jānanyogī muhyati kaścana |\ntasmātsarveṣu kāleṣu yogayukto bhavārjuna ||","read":"naite sritee paartha jaananyogee muhyati kashchana |\ntasmaatsarveshu kaaleshu yogayukto bhavaarjuna ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Knowing these paths, O Pârtha, the Yogi is nowise perplexed. Therefore in all times be firm in yoga, O Arjuna.","en2":"No Yogi, O son of Prithâ, is deluded after knowing these paths. Therefore, O Arjuna, be thou steadfast in Yoga, at all times.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna tells Arjuna that one who knows these paths is never confused. So Arjuna should stay steady in this practice at all times."},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"वेदेषु यज्ञेषु तपःसु चैव ।\nदानेषु यत्पुण्यफलं प्रदिष्टम् ।\nअत्येति तत्सर्वमिदं विदित्वा ।\nयोगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यम् ॥","iast":"vedeṣu yajñeṣu tapaḥsu caiva |\ndāneṣu yatpuṇyaphalaṃ pradiṣṭam |\natyeti tatsarvamidaṃ viditvā |\nyogī paraṃ sthānamupaiti cādyam ||","read":"vedeshu yajneshu tapahsu chaiva |\ndaaneshu yatpunyaphalam pradishtam |\natyeti tatsarvamidam viditvaa |\nyogee param sthaanamupaiti chaadyam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The fruit of meritorious deeds, attached in the Vedas to sacrifices, to austerities, and also to almsgiving, the Yogî passeth all these by having known this, and goeth to the supreme and ancient Seat.","en2":"Whatever meritorious effect is declared (in the Scriptures) to accrue from (the study of) the Vedas, (the performance of) Yajnas, (the practice of) austerities and gifts,—above all this rises the Yogi, having known this, and attains to the primeval, supreme Abode.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":"Krishna says the one who knows this goes beyond all the good rewards of the Vedas, of sacrifices, of self-discipline and of giving gifts, and reaches the highest, most ancient home."}];
